        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1079",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\text{det}(A)$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-6 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
